{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/cor-hecke-length-limit-page-vanishing","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Corollary","doco:Section"],"label":"cor:hecke-length-limit-page-vanishing","kind":"corollary","title":"Vanishing above the diagonal of the length-filtered limit page, at every $n$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-gb-spectral-sequence","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-spectral-sequence-collapse"],"cites":["references/dipper-james1986","references/weibel1994"],"tags":["spectral-sequence","hochschild","coxeter-length","shell-condensation"],"text":"hecke-length-limit-page-vanishing.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"cor:hecke-length-limit-page-vanishing\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> be a field of characteristic <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\in R</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[k]_q \\neq 0</code> for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1 \\le k \\le n</code>. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">E_r^{p,q'}</code> be the spectral sequence of the Hochschild complex of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_n(R, q)</code> filtered by Coxeter length, in the bigrading <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q' = k - p</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k</code> the cochain degree (<a href=\"#prop:gb-spectral-sequence\" data-at=\"mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-opener/mass-endomorphism-spectral-shell\">length-filtration spectral sequence</a>). Then</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  E_\\infty^{p, q'} = 0 \\qquad \\text{for all } p \\ge 0,\\ q' > 0 .</code></pre>\n<p><em>This holds for every <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code>. In particular it holds for every real <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q > 1</code> and every <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code>.</em></p>\n<p><em>Proof.</em> The hypothesis on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[k]_q</code> makes <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_n(R, q)</code> semisimple <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"dipper-james1986\">[dipper-james1986]</span>. A semisimple algebra over a field of characteristic <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code> is separable, so <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">HH^k(H_n, H_n) = 0</code> for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k \\ge 1</code> <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"weibel1994\">[weibel1994]</span> (<a href=\"#prop:spectral-sequence-collapse\">limit page for semisimple <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_n</code></a>). The spectral sequence converges with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">E_\\infty^{p,q'} \\cong \\mathrm{gr}^p HH^{p+q'}</code>. For <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p \\ge 0</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q' > 0</code> the total degree <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p + q'</code> is at least <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code>, so <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">E_\\infty^{p,q'} = 0</code>. For real <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q > 1</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[k]_q = (q^k - q^{-k})/(q - q^{-1}) > 0</code>. <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\qquad\\blacksquare</code></p>\n<p><em>At <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n = 3</code> the exact computation gives <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">E_\\infty</code> in cochain degree <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code> only, at filtration degrees <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0, -2, -3</code>; those classes have <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q' = -p \\ge 0</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p \\le 0</code>, consistent with the corollary.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-length-limit-page-vanishing.md","heading":"Corollary","number":"11.1.33","page":"b/cor-hecke-length-limit-page-vanishing","lean":{"expected":true}}
